WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS

Everything in this repository is offered under the MIT terms below, EXCEPT the
items listed under "What it does not cover". That includes the reverse-engineering
notes and knowledge base, the analysis, emulation and diagnostic scripts, the
ColdFire and DSP patch sources, the build tooling, and the documentation. A file
does not need an "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT" tag to be covered; the tag is a
convenience. Where a file carries its own license tag or header, that tag or
header takes precedence over this default.

WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER

  1. Elektron material. This repository contains no Elektron firmware, firmware
     image, or binary (.bin / .syx / .zip), and no Elektron user manual. You
     supply your own copy of the official OS. Firmware built with these tools is
     derived from Elektron's software and is not distributed here; it is not
     licensed by this file.

  2. tools/attic/ (except its README.md). These files are inherited from
     https://github.com/mxldyn/octamax, which ships no license file. They are
     tagged "SPDX-License-Identifier: NONE" and remain the property of their
     author. They are kept here as reverse-engineering cross-reference only, are
     not part of any OT Kyoti FW build, and are offered under GitHub's Terms of
     Service in the same educational spirit as upstream (see CREDITS.md). The
     same applies to any note whose text is explicitly attributed to that
     project (for example reference/upstream-notes.md, which summarises its
     design).

  3. Patches to third-party tools, and everything fetched at build time. The
     *.patch files under tools/ (for example tools/elektron-firmware-tool.patch,
     tools/dsp56300_xcore/vendor.patch and tools/refs/local-patches/) modify
     other projects' code and stay under the license of the project they modify.
     Anything fetched into vendor/ or refs/ keeps its own license (for example
     dsp56300/dsp56300 is GPLv3, and octabam is MIT). Neither directory is
     tracked here beyond its manifests.

  4. Third-party sources are never copied into this repository unless their
     license is compatible with MIT and they carry their own notice. Code under
     GPL-family licenses (including other Paulstretch implementations) may be
     read as a reference but is not to be copied in.

ABOUT THE FIRMWARE FACTS, DISASSEMBLY AND DECOMPILER EXCERPTS

Factual information about the Elektron firmware (memory addresses, byte values,
field offsets, and behavioural descriptions) is stated as fact, and is claimed as
no one's copyrightable expression.

This repository does not include a disassembly or decompilation of the firmware
as a whole, or wholesale listings of it. It does include behavioural pseudocode
restated in our own notation, a small number of closer excerpts of decompiler
output (in NOTES.md), and a few two-instruction "displaced prologue" listings in
reference/, quoted as evidence for individual findings or to document a patch
site. To the extent that any such excerpt is Elektron's expression, it is not
licensed by this file and remains subject to whatever rights Elektron holds in
it. The patch sources in
this repository are our own code and are covered by the MIT terms.

"Elektron" and "Octatrack" are trademarks of Elektron Music Machines MAV AB, used
only to identify the hardware under study. This project is independent and
unofficial, and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Elektron.

